# CODEOWNERS — automatic reviewer routing
#
# Why this exists: branch protection is unavailable on the GitHub Free plan, so
# "every PR reviewed by the owning founder" is honour-system (see docs/11 § CF-20
# and R19, which has recurred 4x). CODEOWNERS does not *enforce* review without
# branch protection, but it does auto-request the right reviewer on every PR, so
# nothing lands on the wrong pair of eyes by omission.
#
# Ownership follows the founder role split (docs/08 § Founder role split):
# Muhammed owns App, Sulaiman owns Platform. Note the execution model — Muhammed
# authors code across both areas; Sulaiman reviews Platform-area PRs and owns the
# underlying decisions. So these entries are about REVIEW, not authorship.
#
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins. Keep the fallback first.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — App founder
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
